16 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Kaplan-Meier survival curve with a red line labeled \215All\216 showing decreasing survival probability over eighty days. Dashed lines indicate median survival near thirty-six days. Below, numbers at risk decrease from two hundred eighty-seven to two across time points.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Horizontal bar chart comparing Lasso model feature weights using mean coefficients from five imputations, showing intubation with the highest positive weight and therapeutic anticoagulation with the highest negative weight, coefficient values on the x-axis.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Two panel image showing model evaluation curves. Left panel: ROC curves comparing Logistic Regression, Random Forest, XGBoost, SVM-RBF, and Gradient Boosting using AUC values; Random Forest achieves the highest AUC of 0.67. Right panel: DCA curves for the same models display net benefit versus threshold probability, with lines closely overlapping indicating similar clinical utility.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Scatterplot illustrates SHAP values for a gradient boosting model, showing the impact of twenty clinical features on model output. Dots are colored by feature value, with blue representing low and pink representing high, and feature importance and directionality are visualized on the horizontal axis.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Side-by-side data visualization showing ROC curve and DCA curve comparisons of four machine learning models: COX, RSF, XGB, and GBSA. Left panel displays ROC curves with XGB achieving the highest AUC of zero point eight five, followed by RSF, GBSA, and COX. Right panel displays decision curve analysis indicating XGB and RSF have higher net benefit across various threshold probabilities compared to COX and GBSA. Legend identifies each model by color.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (SHAP summary plot showing the impact of twenty medical features on the XGBoost model output, with points colored by feature value from low \(blue\) to high \(pink/red\), and features such as vasopressors, prothrombin time, and age displayed along the y-axis.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Panel A displays a Kaplan-Meier survival curve comparing bacterial infection, seasonal influenza with bacterial, and COVID-19 with bacterial groups; survival rates decrease over time and differences are not statistically significant \(p = 0.266\). Panel B presents survival among patients with and without myocardial injury, showing lower survival with myocardial injury and a significant difference \(p = 0.029\). Panel C compares survival for patients with myocardial injury; a significant difference is observed among groups \(p = 0.037\). Panel D compares survival for patients without myocardial injury; no significant difference is observed among groups \(p = 0.305\). Panel E includes six survival curves, stratifying groups by infection type and myocardial injury status; significant differences are observed between groups \(p = 0.022\).) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 45 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
